{"id": 32, "ts": 1792526698.442767, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "agent_1", "message": "I concur with Markus\u2019s move toward **Candidate\u202fD**.\u202fD\u2019s ability to concentrate very well, solve problems extremely well, and take responsibility seriously directly supports the reliability, decision quality, and stress\u2011resilience criteria essential for long\u2011haul flights.\u202fWhile D is described as arrogant and has relatively weak leadership, those traits are less likely to jeopardize safety than the more concrete deficits we see in the other candidates: B\u2019s documented uncooperative, grumpy demeanor and memory weakness for numbers threaten crew cooperation and attention\u2011to\u2011detail; C\u2019s difficulty communicating ideas undermines cockpit information exchange despite his reliability; and A\u2019s tendency to be unorganized and poor at taking criticism raises concerns about operational consistency.\u202fGiven the balance of evidence, D offers the strongest overall safety\u2011critical profile for the long\u2011distance pilot role."}
